        "desc": "This great hall is a chamber of oval shape, in the middle of which is one of the\ntrunks of the great mallorn, tapering towards its crown and yet still making a\npillar of wide girth. The chamber is filled with a soft light; its walls are of\ngreen and silver and its roof of gold. Chairs enough for many elves to be seated\nstand on the wooden floor. Beside the bole of the tree and canopied by a living\nbough stand two thrones, gleaming and glittering in the sparkling light of\nsilver lamps.\n",
